17 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Figure containing two line graphs and two panels of scatter plots. Panel A shows oxygen consumption rate \(OCR\) over time for control and SAM.1 samples with drug additions marked. Panel B presents six scatter plots comparing non-mitochondrial respiration, basal respiration, maximum respiration, H+ proton leak, ATP production, and spare respiratory capacity between control and SAM.1, with statistical significance indicated. Panel C shows extracellular acidification rate \(ECAR\) over time for both groups, with points marking the addition of glucose, oligomycin, and 2-DG. Panel D displays six scatter plots for glycolysis metrics between control and SAM.1, noting significant and non-significant differences.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Composite scientific figure with three panels: \(A\) Western blot images of AKT, mTOR, p70S6, 4E-BP1, and tubulin in different experimental groups; \(B\) three overlaid flow cytometry histogram plots for CD25, IFN-gamma, and TNF-alpha expression in four conditions; \(C\) three bar graphs showing mean fluorescence intensity \(MFI\) for CD25, IFN-gamma, and TNF-alpha under control, SAM.1, and SAM.1 plus rapamycin treatments, indicating significant differences with asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Illustration showing hydrogel interacting with integrin receptors on a cell membrane, activating the PI3K-AKT-mTOR signaling pathway, leading to phosphorylation of 4E-BP1, increased protein synthesis, and mitochondrial activity, with outputs such as IFN-gamma, TNF-alpha, and perforin.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
